&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/rubrik-inc/mycompany/verification/&quot;&gt;Linkedin&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/rubrikinc&quot;&gt;X (formerly Twitter)&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/rubrikinc/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.rubrik.com&quot;&gt;Rubrik.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Inclusion @ Rubrik&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Rubrik, we are dedicated to fostering a culture where people from all backgrounds are valued, feel they belong, and believe they can succeed. Our commitment to inclusion is at the heart of our mission to secure the world’s data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to hire and promote the best talent, regardless of background. We continually review our hiring practices to ensure fairness and strive to create an environment where every employee has equal access to opportunities for growth and excellence. We believe in empowering everyone to bring their authentic selves to work and achieve their fullest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our inclusion strategy focuses on three core areas of our business and culture:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Our Company: We are committed to building a merit-based organization that offers equal access to growth and success for all employees globally. Your potential is limitless here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Culture: We strive to create an inclusive atmosphere where individuals from all backgrounds feel a strong sense of belonging, can thrive, and do their best work. Your contributions help us innovate and break boundaries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Our Communities: We are dedicated to expanding our engagement with the communities we operate in, creating opportunities for underrepresented talent and driving greater innovation for our clients. Your impact extends beyond Rubrik, contributing to safer and stronger communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer/Veterans/Disabled&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Rubrik provides equal employment opportunities to employees and applicants in all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, training, leave, and termination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik provides reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities in accordance with applicable law. If you need an accommodation to participate in the application process or to perform your job, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:hr@rubrik.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;hr@rubrik.com&lt;/a&gt;. Accommodations may include changes to the application process, documents in an alternate format, a sign language interpreter, or specialized equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO IS THE LAW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/olms/regs/compliance/eo_posters/employeerightsposter2page_19final.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;NOTIFICATION OF EMPLOYEE RIGHTS UNDER FEDERAL LABOR LAWS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;About the Team &amp;amp; Role&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik&#39;s Product Line Sales organization drives focused growth across Rubrik&#39;s specialized workloads, including our Unstructured data protection and security portfolio. This team partners closely with core Account Executives, Sales Engineers, and Customer Success to bring deep product and technical expertise into every Unstructured opportunity — from first conversation through technical validation to close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring an NCD Product Line Sales Specialist to own and accelerate Rubrik&#39;s Unstructured data protection business within a defined territory. This is a highly technical, quota-carrying overlay role: you&#39;ll be the subject-matter expert who can go deep on NAS storage architectures, file-generating applications, backup and recovery mechanics, and the security behind protecting these growing assets — and use that fluency to win deals against competitive point solutions. The ideal candidate has sold in this exact space before, at a company like NetApp, Dell, Qumulo, Vast, EverPure, Komprise, Superna, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the NCD product line number: &lt;/strong&gt;partner with core Account Executives to identify, qualify, and close NCD data protection and security opportunities across net-new and existing accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead with technical credibility: &lt;/strong&gt;articulate Rubrik’s NCD architecture, security posture, and the gaps in storage native shared snapshot protection in a way that resonates with both technical and business buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive technical discovery and validation: &lt;/strong&gt;run or co-lead discovery calls, demos, and proof-of-concept engagements for NCD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Win competitive deals: &lt;/strong&gt;build and defend positioning against competition or &quot;do-nothing&quot;, translating technical differentiation into business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build territory and account plans: &lt;/strong&gt;develop a coverage strategy in partnership with core sales, SE, and channel teams to maximize NCD attach and expansion within the install base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage multiple stakeholders: &lt;/strong&gt;present to IT administrators, security and compliance teams, and executive economic buyers, tailoring the message to each audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forecast with discipline: &lt;/strong&gt;maintain accurate pipeline and forecast data in Salesforce and participate in regular business reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay current: &lt;/strong&gt;maintain deep knowledge of Rubrik’s NCD roadmap, storage ecosystems, and the competitive landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Experience You’ll Need&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Storage sales experience: &lt;/strong&gt;3+ years of quota-carrying sales experience selling storage infrastructure (file preferred) with a deep understanding of these technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Directly relevant background: &lt;/strong&gt;experience at a NAS or file storage vendor such as NetApp, Dell, Qumulo, or VAST (or a comparable company like Komprise, Superna, or EverPure) is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Genuine technical depth: &lt;/strong&gt;comfortable discussing NAS architectures (NetApp ONTAP, Dell PowerScale/Isilon, Qumulo, VAST), SMB/NFS protocols, snapshots and replication, file-generating applications, and ransomware and compliance requirements for unstructured data without relying solely on a Sales Engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven technical selling motion: &lt;/strong&gt;a track record of running or co-leading technical discovery, sizing, and proof-of-concept engagements for storage or data protection solutions, not just handing off to a technical resource.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consultative approach: &lt;/strong&gt;comfortable navigating complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles across storage and infrastructure teams, security, and executive buyers in mid-market and enterprise accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overlay/specialist experience: &lt;/strong&gt;prior success working in a platform-selling model alongside core Account Executives, Sales Engineers, and Customer Success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Track record: &lt;/strong&gt;consistent history of quota attainment and strong pipeline generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education: &lt;/strong&gt;bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on familiarity with enterprise NAS platforms, data management or tiering tools, and backup and recovery workflows for large unstructured data sets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling a data security or resiliency platform that spans on-premises, cloud, and SaaS workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with storage, infrastructure, security, or compliance buyers in target accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-CG1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
