&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finance Manager, GTM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the center of a fast-scaling GTM org on an AI-native transformation journey. You&#39;ll be expected to keep pace with rapid growth, bring order to ambiguity, and continuously challenge how the finance function operates — not just run the existing playbook. The Finance Manager will report to Director Finance, and they will own financial reporting to finance and sales leaders. They will manage Headcount, T&amp;amp;E expense, and support key deliverables like annual planning, bookings forecast, BvA analysis, monthly/quarterly financial reporting and ad hoc analysis of the business. We are looking for an AI-native leader who treats AI as a default part of their workflow — automating recurring reporting, building self-serve analytics, and using LLM-based tools to move faster and go deeper than a traditional finance function.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position will be based in Palo Alto, California and will require in-office attendance 3 days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Partner with the Chief Business Officer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own headcount management and collaborate with Ops and Recruiting to maintain accurate source of truth for actuals &amp;amp; forecasts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Construct &amp;amp; present monthly and quarterly review of various pillars in the and CBO’s org to Sales and Finance Executive Leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bookings by Product / team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expense by type / team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RoI/Cost-benefits ratios&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BvA explanations to Finance Executive Leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide ad hoc reporting and analysis for senior management as needed to review and improve business and financial performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior analysts on the team, and construct independent processes that support your work, that analysts can be trained on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Partner with the VP of Sales Ops &amp;amp; VP of Sales Enablement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own headcount management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the SKO, President Club Budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build monthly and quarterly decks with topline and expense insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project Manage the teams’ deliverables around monthly and quarterly close activities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
