&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Rubrik, we are seeking a leader for a strategic cross-functional role responsible for developing and managing the Global Professional Services Partner Enablement program (RPSP). In this critical position, you will develop and manage the program&#39;s entire lifecycle, ensuring that our partners remain compliant with all professional requirements while facilitating deep cross-functional collaboration. You will play a vital part in building the operational foundation that allows our partner ecosystem to scale effectively alongside Rubrik’s growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For this role we want a strategic thinker and experienced leader with a passion for partner success and professional services excellence. The ideal candidate will possess a blend of operational rigor, relationship-building skills, and deep program management expertise.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports To: Vice President, Global Professional Services&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program Leadership: Build and manage the Rubrik Professional Services Partner Enablement program (RPSP), establishing it as a world-class standard for partner excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Governance &amp;amp; Compliance: Drive and enforce program participation requirements to ensure all partners meet Rubrik’s high standards for service delivery and technical proficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner closely with PS Global Practice Leaders, Rubrik University, PS Leadership, and Services Engineering Manager to align enablement goals with business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner Ecosystem Enablement: Collaborate with various enablement teams, including GSI, MSP, and SI partners, to develop and scale specialized partner tracks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifecycle Management: Oversee the end-to-end lifecycle of the RPSP, including recruitment, onboarding, ongoing performance monitoring, and strategic program evolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: 7-10 years of direct experience in Professional Services (PS) partner program development and management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive Presence: Significant experience with executive-level interaction, with a proven ability to influence senior stakeholders and drive strategic program initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry Expertise: Demonstrated success in building and managing partner enablement systems specifically for a Global Professional Services business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organizational Navigability: Extensive experience partnering across diverse global teams and operational boundaries, including GSI, MSP, and SI environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Management, or a related field; equivalent practical experience is welcomed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program Management: Strong understanding of program lifecycles, compliance frameworks, and cross-functional enablement workflows within a global services context.&lt;/li&gt;
