&lt;p&gt;As the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Manager, Channels - Central Region&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be responsible for leading, scaling, and driving the channel go-to-market (GTM) strategy across a high-growth territory spanning the Central United States. You will recruit, mentor, and elevate a team of Channel Development Managers (CDMs) who cultivate strategic relationships with key regional partners, national solution providers, and elite resellers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this senior leadership role, you will act as a critical bridge between Rubrik’s Central channel ecosystem and internal executive stakeholders across Field Sales, Systems Engineering, Global Alliances, Channel Marketing, and Sales Operations. You will own the Central Region&#39;s channel revenue targets, drive joint pipeline generation, and shape high-impact partner strategies that align with Rubrik’s long-term enterprise growth objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Strategy &amp;amp; Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Formulate and execute a comprehensive GTM channel strategy across the Central Region to accelerate revenue growth, expand market share, and maximize partner productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Partner Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish and nurture deep relationships with executive and C-suite leadership across key regional and national partner organizations to keep Rubrik top-of-mind as a strategic vendor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Sales Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with Central Region Sales Leadership to align channel strategies directly with enterprise account plans, joint account mapping, and field sales engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Recruit, coach, and develop a team of Channel Development Managers (CDMs). Drive a culture of accountability, operational excellence, and high performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution &amp;amp; Quota Attainment:&lt;/strong&gt; Guide team execution toward aggressive monthly, quarterly, and annual pipeline generation and revenue targets, stepping in as executive sponsorship on strategic enterprise opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget &amp;amp; MDF Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct and allocate regional Market Development Funds (MDF) and enablement budgets, prioritizing investments that drive measurable ROI, demand generation, and partner loyalty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forecasting &amp;amp; Pipeline Rigor:&lt;/strong&gt; Implement rigorous forecasting, pipeline analytics, and Quarterly Business Reviews (QBRs) to maintain channel visibility, account coverage, and revenue predictability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Mobilize internal resources across Systems Engineering, Alliances, Marketing, and Operations to equip partners with technical enablement, co-selling tools, and deal registration support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience You’ll Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overall Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 7–10 years of progressive experience in enterprise IT Channel Sales, Partner Management, or Strategic Alliances within the cybersecurity, data management, cloud, or SaaS sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years of direct people management experience leading a team of channel sales professionals (CDMs/CAMs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; A consistent track record of exceeding multi-million-dollar regional quotas, accelerating partner revenue, and driving joint enterprise sales campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep expertise in partner business models, GTM planning, target account selling, and consultative solution-selling techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Presence:&lt;/strong&gt; Outstanding written and verbal communication skills with the confidence to influence partner executives and internal cross-functional leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Ecosystem Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong familiarization with the Central US partner ecosystem (VARs, MSPs, Systems Integrators, and National Partners).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s Degree in Business, Marketing, Computer Science, or related field preferred (or equivalent practical experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Values:&lt;/strong&gt; A strong role model for Rubrik’s core values—fostering cross-functional collaboration, strategic thinking, and an inclusive, winning team culture.&lt;/li&gt;
