&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI API Platform Engineer is a hands-on technical lead who designs and builds the APIs and platform capabilities powering Rubrik&#39;s AI-driven products and automation, owning the full API lifecycle across any stack, cloud, or iPaaS. This role delivers secure, scalable, high-performance APIs and full-stack services while enabling AI-native consumption patterns across the enterprise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and own APIs in any tech stack&lt;/strong&gt; - REST, GraphQL, gRPC, and webhooks - choosing the right language, cloud service, or iPaaS for each use case.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build for AI use cases&lt;/strong&gt;, exposing data/services as tools for LLMs and AI agents, and enabling RAG and agentic workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own core backend engineering &lt;/strong&gt;in Node.js / Java / Python / Go, with strong data modeling and performance tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define API governance &lt;/strong&gt;- versioning, documentation standards, and reusable auth/error-handling/observability frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide technical leadership&lt;/strong&gt; through design reviews, code reviews, and mentoring of engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define NFRs and SLAs&lt;/strong&gt; for availability, latency, throughput, and reliability, and ensure designs meet them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with security and compliance &lt;/strong&gt;to meet regulatory and audit requirements across APIs and integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead technical discovery&lt;/strong&gt; for new API, integration, and AI-enablement initiatives with product and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive reuse and standardizatio&lt;/strong&gt;n through shared APIs, connectors, SDKs, and an integration catalog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluate emerging patterns&lt;/strong&gt; (event-driven integration, AI agent frameworks, low-code automation) to shape the platform roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software engineering experience, with 5+ years in API/full-stack/backend development across multiple languages and clouds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years in a senior/lead/architect capacity owning API and platform designs for complex, enterprise-scale systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years in an FDE role, working directly with internal customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills - API, Fullstack &amp;amp; Backend&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep API expertise across&lt;/strong&gt; REST, including contract-first design (OpenAPI/Swagger) and robust error handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong backend and full-stack skills&lt;/strong&gt; in Node.js / Java / Python / Go, plus platform-agnostic experience across cloud and iPaaS (MuleSoft, Workato, Boomi).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud-native development&lt;/strong&gt; on AWS, Azure, or GCP, including serverless, Kubernetes, and infrastructure as code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong data skills &lt;/strong&gt;- SQL and NoSQL database design, plus integration data formats (JSON, XML, CSV).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure API design&lt;/strong&gt; using OAuth 2.0/OIDC, mTLS, and secrets management, with solid CI/CD and Git-based workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SaaS integration&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;experience&lt;/strong&gt; with platforms such as NetSuite, Workday, Salesforce, or Snowflake.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;API Gateway expertise&lt;/strong&gt; with platforms such as Kong / Apigee / AWS API Gateway / Azure APIM / MuleSoft API Gateway for routing, rate limiting, and policy enforcement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;API testing proficiency &lt;/strong&gt;using tools such as Postman for functional, and regression testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Networking fundamentals, &lt;/strong&gt;including VPN/VPC concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of DevOps practices and toolchains&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills - AI &amp;amp; Intelligent Platform Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on experience with the AI-assisted SDLC&lt;/strong&gt; - using AI tools to design, build, test, and manage APIs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience building APIs for AI consumption&lt;/strong&gt;, including function/tool-calling interfaces for LLMs and agents.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working knowledge of AI/LLM frameworks&lt;/strong&gt; (OpenAI, Anthropic, LangChain) and vector databases, and how they integrate with enterprise APIs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understanding of AI-specific NFRs&lt;/strong&gt; - latency, cost, rate limiting, and safety/guardrails.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practical experience with AI coding assistants&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g., GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Claude Code) for AI assisted platform and infrastructure development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
