&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The&lt;strong&gt; Senior AI Evals Test Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; is a hands-on technical role responsible for defining, developing, and executing robust evaluation frameworks and test strategies for AI agents built using the &lt;strong&gt;Google Agent Development Kit (ADK) or similar sort of agentic frameworks&lt;/strong&gt;. This role bridges AI development and reliable deployment — ensuring our agents are safe, ethical, effective, and meet high-quality performance standards. A significant focus of the role is on Responsible AI and Safety Evals, including &lt;strong&gt;adversarial testing, red-teaming, bias detection, and toxicity measurement&lt;/strong&gt;. The engineer will &lt;strong&gt;design scalable evaluation pipelines&lt;/strong&gt;, build synthetic test environments, and work closely with AI/ML Engineers, Researchers, and policy teams to ensure agents are production-ready and compliant with regulatory and ethical standards. The role is &lt;strong&gt;70% Automation and 30% Manual Testing&lt;/strong&gt;, and sits within the &lt;strong&gt;Applied AI: Test Engineering team&lt;/strong&gt; as a key technical authority.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and build agent evaluation frameworks &lt;/strong&gt;— create end-to-end infrastructure for evaluating LLM-based agents across correctness, latency, cost, safety, and task completion rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build synthetic testing environments and simulation strategies&lt;/strong&gt; to stress-test AI agents under diverse real-world conditions, with specific focus on agents built on Google ADK and related Google AI/ML services (e.g., Vertex AI, Gemini models)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build golden datasets and test harnesses&lt;/strong&gt; — curate domain-specific evaluation sets for Rubrik&#39;s product verticals (data security, SaaS protection, cyber recovery, compliance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish eval-as-a-service&lt;/strong&gt; — build and enhance centralized evaluation platform that any IT team members can self-serve to test their agents against standardized and custom benchmarks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automate regression and drift detection&lt;/strong&gt; — implement CI/CD-integrated eval pipelines that catch regressions on every model or prompt change before production deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define eval taxonomies and rubrics&lt;/strong&gt; — establish structured scoring criteria for agentic workflows (tool use accuracy, multi-step reasoning, hallucination rate, policy adherence, error recovery)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instrument production observability &lt;/strong&gt;— build real-time monitoring for agent quality in production: success rates, user corrections, fallback triggers, escalation patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benchmark and select models&lt;/strong&gt; — run structured model comparisons (cost, quality, latency trade-offs) to inform model selection decisions across agent use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analyze and interpret evaluation results&lt;/strong&gt;, providing clear, actionable quality and safety reports to stakeholders and development teams, with specific focus on risk metrics, trend analysis, and mitigation recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define comprehensive end-to-end QA strategies &lt;/strong&gt;— functional, integration, regression, and user acceptance testing (UAT) — tailored for conversational and goal-oriented AI agents with tool-use, memory, and multi-turn reasoning capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and maintain detailed test artifacts&lt;/strong&gt; (test plans, test cases, test scenarios, automated test suites) covering agent features, tool invocation, memory persistence, and reasoning accuracy across evolving model versions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify, document, prioritize, and track defects&lt;/strong&gt;, performance regressions, and alignment failures using Jira, collaborating closely with Applied AI Engineers to analyze root causes and validate fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluate new technologies and patterns&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g., new tools for Agent Evals), run proofs-of-concept, and influence the platform roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with policy and legal teams&lt;/strong&gt; to ensure agent evaluations systematically cover regulatory compliance, fairness objectives, and emerging AI governance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide technical leadership to engineers&lt;/strong&gt;, including solutioning, design reviews, code reviews, pair programming, and mentoring of junior and contract engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally &lt;/strong&gt;— work closely with ML engineers, product teams, platform engineers, and security to embed eval-driven quality gates into the agent development lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years of overall software Test engineering experience&lt;/strong&gt;, with 5+ years focused on test engineering, QA automation, or developer tooling, and demonstrated ability to build evaluation systems across multiple AI/ML domains, conversational agents, or Large Language Models (LLMs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2+ years working with ML/AI systems, building&lt;/strong&gt;, testing, or evaluating models in production environments, including hands-on experience with LLM-based applications, prompt engineering, RAG pipelines, or agentic workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2+ years as a senior/lead, owning evaluation strategy,&lt;/strong&gt; quality frameworks, and technical decisions for complex AI agent systems in an enterprise product environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1+ years &lt;/strong&gt;in designing or operating evaluation frameworks specifically for generative AI / LLM agents, including benchmarking, red-teaming, and production quality monitoring in the AI ADLC model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep hands-on experience with LLM evaluation&lt;/strong&gt; — familiarity with frameworks and libraries such as LangSmith, DeepEval,LLM as a Judge, Promptfoo, RAGAS, Hugging Face evaluation tooling, custom eval harnesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong understanding of agentic AI patterns &lt;/strong&gt;— tool use, function calling, multi-step planning, ReAct/CoT reasoning chains, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production experience with eval pipelines &lt;/strong&gt;— building automated, CI-integrated evaluation infrastructure (not just notebooks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proficiency in Python&lt;/strong&gt; — strong scripting and tooling skills; experience with pytest, async patterns, and data processing at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Familiarity with Google Cloud Platform (GCP) or any Cloud Service&lt;/strong&gt; relevant to AI/ML (e.g., Vertex AI) and experience integrating testing into MLOps workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statistical literacy&lt;/strong&gt; — ability to design experiments, interpret eval metrics with appropriate confidence, and avoid common pitfalls (overfitting to benchmarks, metric gaming)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise product sensibility&lt;/strong&gt; — understanding of how AI quality translates to customer trust in a B2B/enterprise context (security, compliance, reliability SLAs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent communication&lt;/strong&gt; — ability to present eval results and quality trade-offs to engineering leadership, articulate risks and safety findings to non-technical audiences, and drive alignment on ship/no-ship decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on experience with CI/CD pipelines and Git-based workflows&lt;/strong&gt;, including automated testing, static analysis, deployment automation, and environment configuration for our DevTestOps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech Stack:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Python(Must), TypeScript, Java (Optional)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test Automation:Selenium, Playwright&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LLM Providers:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Anthropic Claude, OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, open-source models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Eval Tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; DeepEvals(Must), LLM as a Judge (Must), Promptfoo/RAGAS/LangSmith/ Custom harnesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent Evals Frameworks/libraries:&lt;/strong&gt; LangGraph, Claude Agent SDK, custom orchestrators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt;DevOps (Basic), Kubernetes, CI/CD (Jenkins/GitHub Actions), observability stacks (Datadog/Grafana)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep Learning/NLP Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;: Fundamental understanding of how LLMs work, including concepts like RAG, prompting, and the technical challenges related to alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with data analysis and visualization tools (e.g., Pandas, SQL) for analyzing evaluation and safety results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Policy Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with AI ethics principles and industry standards for responsible AI development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Garbage-in/Garbage-out (GIGO) Tools&lt;/strong&gt;: Any tool or framework that specializes in testing the model&#39;s response to highly ambiguous, misleading, or malformed inputs to test for robustness and safety failures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience testing complex APIs,&lt;/strong&gt; especially for tool-integration and function-calling scenarios in agentic workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with prompt injection (Must)&lt;/strong&gt; and data poisoning skills is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Certifications in AI/ML&lt;/strong&gt;, cloud platforms (GCP, AWS), AWS Machine Learning Specialty, Google Professional ML Engineer, DeepLearning.AI specializations and software testing methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven ability to lead without direct authority&lt;/strong&gt;, influencing cross-functional teams and driving technical decisions through clarity and data rather than hierarchy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience working in agile environments&lt;/strong&gt;, collaborating closely with product owners, scrum teams, and distributed stakeholders across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent communication and documentation skills&lt;/strong&gt;, comfortable presenting solutions and trade-offs to engineers, managers, and senior business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong architectural thinking and problem-solving skills&lt;/strong&gt;, including the ability to decompose complex business processes into simple solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating agents in cybersecurity, data protection, or infrastructure domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Rubrik&#39;s product portfolio or similar enterprise data management platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on with human-in-the-loop eval workflows (annotation platforms, inter-rater reliability)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with model fine-tuning evaluation (pre/post quality comparison)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in building internal developer platforms or tooling teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to open-source eval frameworks or published work on AI evaluation methodology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive red-teaming and adversarial testing — design adversarial evaluation suites for jailbreak resistance, data leakage prevention, and boundary enforcement in enterprise-grade agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join Us in Securing and Accelerating the World&#39;s AI Transformation&lt;/h2&gt;
