&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Applied AI Engineer to join Rubrik&#39;s Applied AI team, building production-grade, full-stack applications and APIs for our internal Business teams while embedding AI-agentified capabilities into these internal platforms. This is a hands-on build role: you will own features end to end — from database schema through backend services and distributed systems to the user interface — and bring practical, hands-on experience building or integrating AI agents, tool-calling workflows, or LLM-powered features into production systems that our business stakeholders rely on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines strong full-stack engineering fundamentals with a systems mindset for reliability and scale, and has spent meaningful hands-on time (1–2 years) building AI-agentified applications — not just experimenting with AI tools, but shipping agentic features in production. We are targeting 8+ years of overall software engineering experience; this is flexible for candidates who demonstrate strong depth across full-stack, distributed systems, and applied AI during technical evaluation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own features end to end — database schema, backend services, APIs, and frontend (React/Next.js) user interface — operating as an owner rather than a ticket-taker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build full-stack web applications: responsive, production-grade frontends using React/Next.js, backed by well-designed REST APIs and backend services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build APIs and services that are consumed by applications, internal tools, and AI agents/LLMs, including tool-calling interfaces..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and productionize AI-agentified features — agentic workflows, LLM-powered automation, and AI-assisted tooling — grounded in 1–2 years of hands-on experience with these systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect for distributed systems concerns: scalability, fault tolerance, data consistency, and service boundaries across backend and data layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply reliability engineering practices — observability (logging, metrics, tracing), SLAs/SLOs, incident response, and post-incident reviews — to keep production systems healthy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and optimize relational database schemas, including joins, indexing, and query performance tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build clean, well-tested, production-grade frontend and backend code that others can read, test, and extend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clarify requirements upfront, surface blockers early, and communicate progress proactively without being asked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate openly with internal Business stakeholders, Product, QA, DevOps, and UX or designer teams; avoid working in silos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Education &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of hands-on software engineering experience across full-stack development (flexible based on demonstrated strength in technical evaluation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1–2 years of hands-on experience building, integrating, or operating AI-agentified applications (agentic workflows, tool-calling, RAG, or LLM-powered features) in production..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning systems designed for scale and reliability, not just feature delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Technical Skills — Applied AI&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1–2 years of hands-on experience building AI-agentified applications, including agent frameworks (e.g., LangChain, LangGraph, ADK, or equivalent), tool/function-calling for LLMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of AI-specific considerations: latency, cost, rate limiting, and safety/guardrails when exposing systems for AI consumption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI-assisted development tools (e.g., Claude Code or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Technical Skills — Full Stack&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frontend: Strong JavaScript fundamentals; hands-on experience with React and Next.js for building modern, production-grade web applications (hooks, state management, component architecture, routing/SSR).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backend: Proficient in Python, writing production-grade code; hands-on experience with FastAPI or Flask (or equivalent frameworks) for building REST APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Database: Experience with relational and non-relational databases (PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server, MongoDB or equivalent); solid understanding of schema design, joins, indexing, and query optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Technical Skills — Distributed Systems &amp;amp; Reliability&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of distributed systems concepts: service decomposition, consistency models, caching, queuing/messaging, and failure handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliability engineering fundamentals: observability (logging, metrics, tracing), SLAs/SLOs, error budgets, and operational runbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to reason about system design trade-offs and build scalable, resilient solutions under ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Soft Skills&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive communication — shares updates without being asked and flags blockers early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Asks the right questions — clarifies requirements upfront before jumping into implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership mindset — treats the project as their own rather than just completing tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transparency — speaks up when something is unclear instead of making assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset to break down complex or ambiguous problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with agentic frameworks (ADK, LangGraph, or similar) beyond individual projects — production deployment experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with API documentation standards (Swagger/OpenAPI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic DevOps awareness (Docker, CI/CD) and Git/version-control best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Testing experience across unit and integration levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern web app tooling — component libraries (e.g., Tailwind, MUI) and state management (e.g., Redux, Zustand).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to cloud-native development (AWS, Azure, or GCP), including containers and infrastructure as code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join Us in Securing and Accelerating the World&#39;s AI Transformation&lt;/h2&gt;
