&lt;h2&gt;About the team:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik&#39;s mission is to secure and accelerate the world&#39;s AI transformation. IT is where we apply that to ourselves. We&#39;re moving Rubrik&#39;s own enterprise off a traditional application stack and onto an intelligent one.&lt;br&gt;Our goal is what we call the Thinking Enterprise: applications that run the business instead of just recording it. They learn from our data, act through our agents, and improve with each decision. That work is already underway, and we&#39;d like you to help build it.&lt;br&gt;We build the internal products our Accounting, Controllership, and Tax teams use every day, the tools that decide how fast we close the books and how much we can trust the numbers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In our approach to accounting, agents understand the chart of accounts, the accounting policy, and the transaction in front of them, and they carry an entry from the source event through to a posted, audit-ready record.&lt;br&gt;If you&#39;re curious about why every task on the close calendar sits where it does, and whether most of those tasks can be run by agents as the work happens, so that only the final close needs to be locked down and compliant; if you know which steps can be questioned and rebuilt and which must follow the rules every time; and if you&#39;re excited about shortening the close by removing manual effort, then you&#39;re in the right place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead product strategy for accounting (general ledger, close, intercompany, reconciliations, fixed assets, Sub-ledger accounting, and commissions), rebuilding rather than patching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring an AI-first approach, introducing agents, evals, and automation into real accounting workflows with audit-level stakes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design how agents are built and tested: break complex accounting work into well-scoped steps, define evals, and set clear human-in-the-loop checkpoints for approvals and audit-sensitive decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply first-principles thinking, taking a legacy close task, asking why it exists, and building what replaces it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision and roadmap for next-generation accounting capabilities, from journal entry to financial statements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype quickly with AI tools, validating logic, data flows, and control points before engineering engages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with finance system developers (onsite and offshore), AI architects, Internal Audit, and vendors to turn prototypes into scalable, SOX-compliant products; lead UAT, training, and adoption through go-live and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Experience you&#39;ll need:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience building accounting or financial products at a product company, on Oracle, SAP, or Workday Financials, as a product manager, product owner, or architect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on delivery of AI-enabled or agentic workflows in an enterprise. Even if you&#39;ve taken only one module to production, you can explain how you broke it down, how you evaluated it, and where the model did and didn&#39;t earn its keep.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of accounting principles (US GAAP, ASC 606) and the end-to-end close. We&#39;re looking for people who understand the full capability, not just operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years across product management, finance systems, or accounting operations in enterprise, or a body of work that speaks louder than the year count.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of turning complicated accounting and finance problems into simple, scalable products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SOX and audit fluency, and experience leading onsite/offshore delivery teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with AI tooling: you use AI-assisted coding and low-code tools to prototype and test ideas quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, with the ability to align Controllership, Tax, Accounting Operations, Internal Audit, and executive leadership (including CFO staff) behind a bold direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: NetSuite, Xactly, and Blackline/FloQast experience; working knowledge of P2P and O2C.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The minimum and maximum base salaries for this role are posted below; additionally, the role is eligible for bonus potential, equity and benefits. The range displayed reflects the minimum and maximum target for new hire salaries for the role based on U.S. location. Within the range, the salary offered will be determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$163,200&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$244,800 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join Us in Securing and Accelerating the World&#39;s AI Transformation&lt;/h2&gt;
