&lt;h3 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Staff Product Manager, Databases&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; US - Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik (NYSE: RBRK) is the Security and AI Operations Company, delivering one platform built at the intersection of data, identity, and AI. The platform enables agentic cyber resilience and trusted AI operations for enterprises worldwide, built to recover before disruption strikes and stay a step ahead, so security is never the reason ambition stalls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Product Management Team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Rubrik, our Product Management team is at the forefront of defining the strategy and driving execution to strengthen our leading platform for cyber-resilience. We are dedicated to meeting the ever-changing data management and security needs of our customers and wear multiple hats throughout the different stages in the product lifecycle and set the vision for our growing family of products. As advocates for both our users and our business, Product Managers balance varied perspectives and empower their teams to do great work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When a bank or a hospital loses a critical database to ransomware or a bad change, nobody asks about backup schedules. They ask how fast it&#39;s back and whether they can trust what came back. Your job is to make Rubrik the answer to both questions for Oracle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the Databases product team with Oracle as your first focus, and own it end to end, from strategy to the outcomes customers see. Oracle is one of the hardest workloads we protect. Our customers run their most important systems on it. You&#39;ll also lead work that spans several databases, with the PMs who own them as partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an individual contributor role reporting to the Director of Product Management, Databases. You&#39;ll work with engineering teams in the US and India.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Oracle roadmap.&lt;/strong&gt; Set how Rubrik protects and recovers Oracle across RAC, Exadata, Data Guard, on-premises and cloud. Weigh recovery speed against data loss and effort, and make the call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the product voice with customers.&lt;/strong&gt; Run deep dives with DBAs, present to executives when the stakes are high, and explain where Rubrik fits next to Oracle&#39;s own tools and other vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn escalations into product.&lt;/strong&gt; When a restore matters, you&#39;re on the call for product, alongside support, engineering and the customer&#39;s DBAs and executives. Bring a plan, then fix the cause in the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive work across databases.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead initiatives that span several databases, such as recovering whole applications in the right order and proving that backups restore, and help decide which databases we protect next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Choose with evidence.&lt;/strong&gt; Use customer conversations, usage and support data to make the business case for what to build and what to defer. Write requirements engineers trust, with your reasoning shown.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Launch and land.&lt;/strong&gt; Give sales engineers the positioning and training they need, and join the field on large enterprise deals. Work with partners such as Oracle and Everpure, and track adoption after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In 3 months,&lt;/strong&gt; you&#39;ve met customers, sales engineers and support. You know where Oracle protection works well and where customers need more, and you&#39;ve written your view of the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In 6 months,&lt;/strong&gt; you&#39;re the go-to person for Oracle at Rubrik, and your roadmap shapes what engineering builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In 12 months,&lt;/strong&gt; you&#39;ve shipped improvements Oracle customers notice. You&#39;re leading a cross-database initiative with engineering, and you&#39;ve fixed the root cause of a problem customers kept raising.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Oracle backup and recovery. You can explain how RMAN backups, archived redo logs and point-in-time recovery work, and what Data Guard and RAC change. You&#39;ve run Oracle in production, supported it or built products for it, and you can go deep on architecture with engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Typically 8+ years of product management for technical enterprise products, or equivalent years as a DBA, solutions architect or sales engineer whose calls changed what a team built or bought. You don&#39;t need a PM title, but tell us what you changed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort in front of customers at every level, from a room of DBAs to a CIO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, precise writing and speaking. You can turn a messy situation into a short doc that gets a decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A zero-to-one mindset. You&#39;ll write the plan for work that doesn&#39;t have one yet, and do what needs doing whatever your title says.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with AI tools in how you research and write.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Exadata, Oracle Database Appliance, or Oracle Database on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI), AWS or Azure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with other enterprise databases, such as SQL Server, PostgreSQL or Db2.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in data protection, disaster recovery or cyber resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with customers in banking, insurance, healthcare or government.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not match every line. If you&#39;ve owned recovery for another enterprise database or for storage, and you&#39;ve worked with Oracle, apply and tell us how you&#39;d learn the rest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-NM2&lt;/p&gt;
